{"nodes": [{"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_gems_manual_po_plan", "label": "GEMS QCF to Manual PO Implementation Plan", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_gems_manual_po_flow_flag", "label": "GEMS_MANUAL_PO_FLOW kill switch", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A one-month pilot must revert by flipping one value with no redeploy, rollback migration or code change. An env var was chosen over config_autopo (read by the external import-pr cron, unverifiable risk) and over a feature_flags table (too much machinery). The cost is that toggling requires restarting both deployment units.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_isgemsmanualpoenabled", "label": "isGemsManualPoEnabled", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Fail-closed and synchronous: unset, empty or unparseable resolves to off, because absence of configuration must never enable a pilot feature. Kept as the single read point so storage can move to a DB flag later without touching call sites.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_qcfworkflowpolicy", "label": "qcfWorkflowPolicy", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Centralizes the GEMS rules because GEMS behavior is currently only a side effect of seeded configuration; every function takes rows loaded from the database, never request body fields, and returns a structured result so callers can map 403 vs 409.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_waiting_manual_po", "label": "WAITING_MANUAL_PO milestone 26", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The dashboard mapping stays permanent even after rollback: the flag gates transitions, not interpretation, and rows that reached milestone 26 during the pilot have real Manual POs in SAP. It is terminal, since nothing writes po_number back.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_dashboard_status_waiting_manual_po", "label": "DASHBOARD_STATUS.WAITING_MANUAL_PO", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A new dashboard status string rather than reusing 'Waiting CS', so seven role-scoped label maps and their milestone group arrays each need an entry or GEMS rows fall through unmapped.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_sub_category_id_migration", "label": "qcf_library.sub_category_id migration", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Backfill must run before the FK or the constraint fails on pre-existing orphans; ON DELETE SET NULL rather than CASCADE so deleting a category cannot destroy QCF history. Dev probe shows only 2.3% of rfq_library rows carry the source value, so the feature would launch degraded.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_buildgemsmanualporecipients", "label": "buildGemsManualPoRecipients", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_normalizeemailrecipients", "label": "normalizeEmailRecipients", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Defense in depth for all existing email callers, not a substitute for the purpose-specific resolver; it changes behavior for every email in the system so it lands with its own tests.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_generategemsmanualpolink", "label": "generateGemsManualPoLink", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The existing token lookup keys on QCF number plus vendor code only, so writing a CS token today would overwrite the CL token row; the lookup must also match user_type and config_condition and store the CS token as a separate row.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_qcf_cs_token_middleware", "label": "Strict CS QCF token middleware", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The existing middleware validates only JWT signature and expiry and never consults qcf_token_email, so revoked tokens keep working; the CS route additionally validates stored existence, is_active, stored expiry, stored purpose and matching qcf_number.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_findexpiredmanagementreviewitems", "label": "findExpiredManagementReviewItems", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Its predicate is 'CL approval done AND management_comment is null', which would sweep GEMS rows into Management expiry processing since the GEMS path mints no Management token; excluding GEMS is mandatory, not optional.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_approvebycl", "label": "approveByCL GEMS branch", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Reads the flag at approval time rather than from anything snapshotted at QCF creation, so in-flight QCFs follow whatever the flag says the moment CL clicks approve and no half-migrated population exists. The approval transaction commits before SMTP is attempted.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_inflight_gems_backlog", "label": "In-flight GEMS QCF Stranding", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Eight GEMS rows sit CL-approved awaiting Management; once Management is blocked they become unreachable because CL cannot re-approve and the new path only fires at the moment of CL approval. Deploying with the flag off lets the backlog drain itself, avoiding any data migration.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_two_deployment_units", "label": "Two Deployment Units Hazard", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "app.js and src/cron.js are separate processes with separate environments; if only one gets the flag, HTTP runs the pilot while cron still sweeps GEMS QCFs into Management expiry processing, and that failure is silent.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_cl_ownership_filter_defect", "label": "CL Ownership Filter Silently Drops", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The controller passes a scalar cl_id where the repository expects an object with user_id and role, so user.user_id is undefined and the ownership predicate is never added; combined with the missing route role guard, any authenticated role reaches CL approval logic.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_gems_manual_po_plan", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_gems_qcf_backend_contract", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_gems_manual_po_plan", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_manual_sourcing_manual_sourcing_flow_manual_sourcing_flow", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_gems_manual_po_plan", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_openapi_openapi_aigen_backend_api", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/planning.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_gems_manual_po_plan", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_planning_gems_manual_po_flow_flag", "relati